        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T01:50:30Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): per-operation smoothing, opt-in, in every mill dialect\n\nA document-wide \"Smoothing per operation\" post option (#616), off by\ndefault (byte-identical output). On, each operation states its ask -\na finishing op its own tolerance, a roughing op a fifth of the stock\nit leaves (0.01-0.25 mm) - as PARAM Smoothing / SmoothingMode, and the\nposts write their control's words after the preamble and undo them at\nthe section end:\n\n- Tormach/LinuxCNC G64 P<tol> (back to the header's P after)\n- Fanuc G5.1 Q1 / Q0 (no R level: control-version dependent)\n- Haas G187 P3|P1 E<tol> / G187\n- Siemens CYCLE832(<tol>,_FINISH|_ROUGH,1) / CYCLE832()\n- Heidenhain ISO G62 T<tol> / G62\n- Mazak: named once, no guessed word\n\nSaved as the additive `smoothing` project key; undoable through\nSetPostOptions; a checkbox under the post picker (mill posts).\nPinned by tests/smoothing.rs (4).\n\nFixes #616\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
