        "date": "2026-11-10T02:13:01Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): smoothing asks are bounded - Fanuc names it, finish asks half, rough never over a fifth\n\nReview of #635:\n1. Fanuc's G5.1 Q1 states no tolerance, so it could not hold the op's\n   ask: the post names it once and writes nothing (like Mazak), until a\n   bounded form is stated per control (#614).\n2. The rough ask is stock x 0.2 capped at 0.25 mm with NO floor - the\n   old 0.01 mm floor was 25-100% of a 0.01-0.04 mm allowance.\n3. The finish ask is half the op's tolerance: the path is verified at\n   the tolerance and the control's deviation stacks on it (1.5x, not 2x).\n4. Tests: undo/redo of the switch, the project key round-trip (and no\n   key when off), and the reset before the program end.\nAlso: the Heidenhain comment names ISO G62; Tormach's header and reset\nshare one blending constant.\n\nRefs #616\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
